T2. Theorem Y as a 2-adic theta / q-Pochhammer value; the Tate curve with q = rho^2
  Jacobi triple product: sum_(k in Z) rho^(k^2) = prod (1-rho^(2m))(1+rho^(2m-1))^2 mod 2^4000: True
  square-swap word:  Phi_2(Y)    = -1 - 512/(3^9-2^10) - (256/3^9) sum_(k>=1) rho^(k^2)    mod 2^3000: True
  pronic-swap word:  Phi_2(Y_pr) = -1 - 512/(3^9-2^10) - (256/3^9) sum_(k>=1) rho^(k(k+1)) mod 2^3000: True
  j q = 1 + 744 q + 196884 q^2 + 21493760 q^3 + ... (integer coefficients)
  j(rho^2) * rho^2 from the q-expansion  ==  from lambda = theta_2^4/theta_3^4 (mod 2^3940): True
  j(rho^2) * rho^2 is a 2-adic unit: True  =>  v_2(j(rho^2)) = -20; v_2(196884 q) = 2 + 20
  BDGP 1996 (p-adic Mahler-Manin, CITED): j(rho^2) is transcendental; lambda is a rational function
  of theta_3(rho) and psi(rho^2) over Q, so theta_3(rho) and psi(rho^2) are not both algebraic,
  i.e. the square-swap and pronic-swap Bernstein numbers are not both algebraic over Q.
  coefficient ratios: squares rho^((k+1)^2-k^2) = rho * (rho^2)^k (q-hypergeometric, q = rho^2);
  cubes rho^(3k^2+3k+1): exponent quadratic in k, not of the form R(q^k) (no first-order q-difference eq.)
